  "problem": "How many diagonals does a quadrilateral $ABCD$ have?",
  "worked_solution": "Diagonals join non-adjacent vertices.\n\nAs we can see from the diagram below, the diagonals of the quadrilateral are $\\overset{―}{AC}$ and $\\overset{―}{BD}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14133876/assets/9010725d2b0e260cf7ef71eee5adb07b12346727eeffbf8c1fab3efc07310e22.png)\n\nTherefore, the quadrilateral $ABCD$ has $2$ diagonals.",
